{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-js","path":"/posts/skeleton-loaders-for-llm-latency-ngx-skeleton-loader-for-streaming-uis/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1280px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/00711/hero.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.4375%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/fb34c/hero.avif 320w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/646cd/hero.avif 768w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/8b485/hero.avif 1024w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/a73d6/hero.avif 1280w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/a7f9f/hero.avif 1920w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/fb732/hero.avif 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/avif\"\n            /><source\n              srcset=\"/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/cb523/hero.webp 320w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/cd067/hero.webp 768w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/53334/hero.webp 1024w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/4b075/hero.webp 1280w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/f3ff0/hero.webp 1920w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/4293a/hero.webp 2400w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/d4f27/hero.png 320w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/778aa/hero.png 768w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/658fc/hero.png 1024w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/26c69/hero.png 1280w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/7d442/hero.png 1920w,\n/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/00711/hero.png 2400w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/533be9c348e07e10efec760dafa1d198/26c69/hero.png\"\n            alt=\"hero\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>TL;DR; An LLM response has two waits: the silence before the first token and the stream after it. Show <code class=\"language-text\">&lt;ngx-skeleton-loader></code> only for the silence, swap it for the streamed text as soon as the first chunk lands, and drive both phases from one signal 🎉</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>Looking back at 2026, a lot of the UI work around AI features was not about the model at all. It was about <strong>waiting</strong>. A chat answer, a summary, a generated description: they all start with a pause, and then the text arrives piece by piece.</p>\n<p>Most apps treat that as a single \"loading\" state. A spinner spins until the request ends, or the text starts streaming into an empty box with no hint that anything is happening before it. Neither is great.</p>\n<p>In this article, we'll explore how to model the two phases of LLM latency with Angular signals, use <a href=\"https://github.com/willmendesneto/ngx-skeleton-loader\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-skeleton-loader</a> for the first one, and keep screen reader and reduced motion users in mind the whole time. If you want the background on skeletons and perceived performance, I covered it in <a href=\"/posts/ngx-skeleton-loader-states-animations-performance-and-accessibility-for-your-angular-app/\">NGX-Skeleton-Loader — States, Animations, Performance, and Accessibility</a>.</p>\n<h2>The Problem with one \"loading\" flag</h2>\n<p>A streamed LLM response goes through these phases:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>idle</strong>: nothing requested yet;</li>\n<li><strong>waiting</strong>: the request is out, but no token has arrived (time to first token);</li>\n<li><strong>streaming</strong>: tokens keep arriving and the text grows;</li>\n<li><strong>done</strong> or <strong>error</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With a single <code class=\"language-text\">isLoading</code> boolean, you get one of two bad outcomes. Either the skeleton stays on screen while text is already streaming behind it, or there's no feedback during the wait. On top of that, a screen reader can end up announcing every chunk, which is exhausting.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The skeleton answers \"something is coming\". The stream answers \"here it is\". Never show both at once.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>The Solution: one phase signal, two UIs</h2>\n<h4>1. Model the phases with signals</h4>\n<p>The component keeps a <code class=\"language-text\">phase</code> signal and a <code class=\"language-text\">text</code> signal. The first chunk moves the phase from <code class=\"language-text\">waiting</code> to <code class=\"language-text\">streaming</code>. I'm using <code class=\"language-text\">fetch</code> with a streaming endpoint here, but the same state works for any source that gives you chunks, like the Gemini SDKs or the Chrome built-in AI streaming methods.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"typescript\"><pre class=\"language-typescript\"><code class=\"language-typescript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Component<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> DestroyRef<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> inject<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> signal <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'@angular/core'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> NgxSkeletonLoaderComponent <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'ngx-skeleton-loader'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">type</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Phase</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token string\">'idle'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'waiting'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'streaming'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'done'</span> <span class=\"token operator\">|</span> <span class=\"token string\">'error'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator\"><span class=\"token at operator\">@</span><span class=\"token function\">Component</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  selector<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'app-ai-answer'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  imports<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>NgxSkeletonLoaderComponent<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  templateUrl<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'./ai-answer.component.html'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">AiAnswerComponent</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> phase <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token generic-function\"><span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token generic class-name\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>Phase<span class=\"token operator\">></span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'idle'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">readonly</span> text <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">signal</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">''</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">private</span> controller<span class=\"token operator\">?</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> AbortController<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token function\">constructor</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token function\">inject</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>DestroyRef<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">onDestroy</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>controller<span class=\"token operator\">?.</span><span class=\"token function\">abort</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">async</span> <span class=\"token function\">ask</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>prompt<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token builtin\">string</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>controller<span class=\"token operator\">?.</span><span class=\"token function\">abort</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>controller <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">AbortController</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>text<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">''</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>phase<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'waiting'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">try</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> response <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> <span class=\"token function\">fetch</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'/api/answer'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        method<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'POST'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        body<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token constant\">JSON</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">stringify</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> prompt <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        headers<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> <span class=\"token string-property property\">'Content-Type'</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">'application/json'</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n        signal<span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>controller<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>signal<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token operator\">!</span>response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>ok <span class=\"token operator\">||</span> <span class=\"token operator\">!</span>response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>body<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">throw</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Error</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">HTTP </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">${</span>response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>status<span class=\"token interpolation-punctuation punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> reader <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> response<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>body<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">pipeThrough</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">TextDecoderStream</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">getReader</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">while</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token boolean\">true</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> value<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> done <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">await</span> reader<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">read</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>done<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">break</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">phase</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">===</span> <span class=\"token string\">'waiting'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>phase<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'streaming'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>text<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">update</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>current<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> current <span class=\"token operator\">+</span> value<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n      <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>phase<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'done'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">catch</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>error<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n      <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>error <span class=\"token keyword\">as</span> Error<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>name <span class=\"token operator\">!==</span> <span class=\"token string\">'AbortError'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>phase<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">set</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">'error'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, the abort controller covers two unhappy paths: a new question cancels the old stream, and leaving the page doesn't leave a request running.</p>\n<h4>2. Skeleton for the wait, text for the stream</h4>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"html\"><pre class=\"language-html\"><code class=\"language-html\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>section</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">aria-labelledby</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>answer-title<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>h2</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">id</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>answer-title<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>Answer<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>h2</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n\n  @if (phase() === 'waiting') {\n    <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>ngx-skeleton-loader</span>\n      <span class=\"token attr-name\">count</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>3<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span>\n      <span class=\"token attr-name\">animation</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>pulse<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span>\n      <span class=\"token attr-name\">ariaLabel</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>Generating answer<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span>\n      <span class=\"token attr-name\">loadingText</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>Waiting for the first words of the answer<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">/></span></span>\n  }\n\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>div</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">class</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>answer<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">aria-live</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>polite<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">[attr.aria-busy]</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>phase() === 'streaming'<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n    {{ text() }}\n  <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>div</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n\n  @if (phase() === 'error') {\n    <span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;</span>p</span> <span class=\"token attr-name\">role</span><span class=\"token attr-value\"><span class=\"token punctuation attr-equals\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span>alert<span class=\"token punctuation\">\"</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>We couldn't generate an answer. Please try again.<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>p</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span>\n  }\n<span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token tag\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">&lt;/</span>section</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">></span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">count=\"3\"</code> draws three lines, which is roughly the shape of a short answer. That matters: the closer the skeleton is to the final layout, the less the page jumps when the text replaces it. You can tune the shape with <code class=\"language-text\">appearance</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">width</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">height</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">[theme]</code>, and use <code class=\"language-text\">animation=\"pulse\"</code> or the default <code class=\"language-text\">progress</code>.</p>\n<h4>3. What the skeleton already does for accessibility</h4>\n<p>Since the skeleton is visible only while nothing else is, its accessibility matters. <code class=\"language-text\">&lt;ngx-skeleton-loader></code> applies the WAI-ARIA attributes once on the host element: <code class=\"language-text\">role=\"progressbar\"</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">aria-busy</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">aria-valuemin</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">aria-valuemax</code>, <code class=\"language-text\">aria-label</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">aria-valuetext</code>. The individual lines are hidden with <code class=\"language-text\">aria-hidden=\"true\"</code>, so screen readers announce <strong>one</strong> progress bar per component, regardless of <code class=\"language-text\">count</code>.</p>\n<p>The two inputs you'll want to set are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">ariaLabel</code>: the accessible name of the progress bar (defaults to <code class=\"language-text\">loading</code>);</li>\n<li><code class=\"language-text\">loadingText</code>: the value used for <code class=\"language-text\">aria-valuetext</code> (defaults to <code class=\"language-text\">Loading...</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Animations, both built-in and custom ones, are disabled automatically when the user enables the reduce motion preference in the operating system or browser. Nothing to configure there.</p>\n<h4>4. The streamed text: live, but not noisy</h4>\n<p>The text container is the tricky part. Some details to keep in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The live region exists before the text.</strong> The <code class=\"language-text\">div</code> with <code class=\"language-text\">aria-live=\"polite\"</code> is always in the DOM, even when empty. Live regions that appear together with their content are often not announced at all.</li>\n<li><strong><code class=\"language-text\">aria-busy</code> while streaming.</strong> MDN describes <code class=\"language-text\">aria-busy=\"true\"</code> as a way to tell assistive technologies that the region is being updated, so they should wait until it turns <code class=\"language-text\">false</code> before announcing it. When the phase moves to <code class=\"language-text\">done</code>, the binding drops to <code class=\"language-text\">false</code> and the final text can be read as a whole. Screen reader support varies, so test this with the readers your users have.</li>\n<li><strong>Don't move focus to the answer</strong> on every chunk. Let users stay where they are, and offer a clear way to jump to the answer when it's done.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5. Swap, don't stack</h4>\n<p>The <code class=\"language-text\">@if</code> removes the skeleton in the same change detection pass that renders the first chunk. With signals, that happens without manual subscriptions, also in zoneless apps. There's never a frame where the skeleton and the text compete for the same space.</p>\n<p>If you need to delay the skeleton for very fast responses to avoid a flash, add a short timer before switching to <code class=\"language-text\">waiting</code>. Measure your own time to first token before choosing the value.</p>\n<h3>What this gives you</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Honest feedback</strong> for each phase: shape while waiting, text while streaming.</li>\n<li><strong>One signal</strong> as the source of truth, easy to test and easy to reason about.</li>\n<li><strong>Accessibility built in</strong>: one progress bar, a polite live region and reduced motion respected.</li>\n<li><strong>Cancellation</strong> for new prompts and destroyed components.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For the streaming side in more depth, check <a href=\"/posts/streaming-gemini-responses-into-angular-signals/\">Streaming Gemini responses into Angular signals</a>. And if this feature is new in production, put it behind a toggle first, as described in <a href=\"/posts/feature-flagging-gemini-features-in-angular-with-ngx-feature-toggle/\">Feature flagging Gemini features in Angular</a>.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/willmendesneto/ngx-skeleton-loader\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-skeleton-loader on GitHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/ngx-skeleton-loader\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ngx-skeleton-loader on npm</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://angular.dev/guide/signals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Signals on angular.dev</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Guides/Live_regions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">ARIA live regions on MDN</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Reference/Attributes/aria-busy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">aria-busy on MDN</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/prefers-reduced-motion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">prefers-reduced-motion on MDN</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>That’s all for now</h3>\n<p>Latency is part of the AI feature, so design it like one.</p>\n<p>I hope you enjoyed this reading as much as I enjoyed writing it. Thank you so much for reading until the end and see you soon!</p>\n<p>🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Cya 👋</h3>","frontmatter":{"date":"August 24, 2026","path":"/posts/skeleton-loaders-for-llm-latency-ngx-skeleton-loader-for-streaming-uis/","title":"Skeleton loaders for LLM latency — ngx-skeleton-loader for streaming UIs","tags":["ai","angular","accessibility","performance","frontend","gemini"],"status":"active"},"timeToRead":5}},"pageContext":{"postPath":"/posts/skeleton-loaders-for-llm-latency-ngx-skeleton-loader-for-streaming-uis/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["1271460761","63159454"],"slicesMap":{}}